sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ENG as Deletion engine
    participant HOLD as RetentionHold index
    participant CLS as Retention class registry
    participant KEY as Subject key custodian
    participant STORE as Business and document stores
    participant DEV as Attendance devices
    participant AUD as AuditEvent log

    ENG->>HOLD: any active hold on this subject or scope
    HOLD-->>ENG: none active
    ENG->>CLS: floors and ceilings for every class the subject touches
    CLS-->>ENG: floors elapsed for classes A and B, class C floor unset
    Note over ENG,CLS: an unset floor blocks erasure of that class and raises an unresolved-retention flag

    ENG->>STORE: tombstone the multi-subject records in classes A and B
    STORE-->>ENG: tombstones written, payload replaced
    ENG->>DEV: queue biometric erase command per enrolled device
    DEV-->>ENG: acknowledgement per device, or exception state pending
    Note over ENG,DEV: erasure shows complete only on every acknowledgement or an admin attestation of decommission or loss

    ENG->>KEY: destroy the subject data key
    KEY-->>ENG: key destroyed, custodian attests it is outside every backed-up store
    ENG->>STORE: verify sample reads
    STORE-->>ENG: ciphertext only, surrogate-keyed figures still readable
    ENG->>AUD: write decision, basis, mechanism, actor and NTP timestamp
    Note over AUD: the audit record never carries the erased content
    ENG->>ENG: schedule re-evaluation for class C at floor confirmation
